  "description": "The native payload for Agora's local face detection extension, staged out of the AgoraRtcEngine_iOS 4.7.0 archive and packaged for .NET for iOS. Reports whether a face is in frame and how far away it is — used to auto-adjust exposure and capture, or to pause the stream when nobody is there. Add it alongside Net.Agora.Video.iOS, not Net.Agora.Voice.iOS, which lacks a framework this one links — it carries no managed API of its own; the switch that turns it on is AgoraRtcEngineKit.EnableFaceDetection in the RTC binding.",
